WEBVTT

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.640
-Thanks, man.
-Grazie, Guido.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.320
-Guido, what's McQueen's usual?
-(IN ITALIAN)

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.560
How should I know?

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.720
-Perfect. Give me two of them.
-Quiet! My program's on.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.080
Tonight on the Mel Dorado Show...

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.960
His story gripped the world.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.440
Oil billionaire Miles Axlerod,

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.360
in an attempt to become the first car to
circumnavigate the globe without GPS,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.760
ironically ran out of gas,
and found himself trapped in the wild.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.680
Feared dead, he emerged 36 days later,

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.400
running on a fuel he distilled himself
from the natural elements!

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.560
Since then, he's sold his oil fortune,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.560
converted himself from a gas-guzzler
into an electric car

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.800
and has devoted his life to finding
a renewable, clean-burning fuel.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.920
Now he claims to have done it
with his allinol.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.080
And to show the world
what his new super fuel can do

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.400
he's created a racing competition
like no other,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.400
inviting the greatest champions

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.520
to battle in the first ever
World Grand Prix.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.760
Welcome, Sir Miles Axlerod.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.880
Thank you, Mel. It is good to be here.
Listen to me.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.160
Big oil. It costs a fortune.
Pollution is getting worse.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.760
I mean, it's a fossil fuel.
"Fossil," as in dead dinosaurs.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.600
And we all know
what happened to them.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.440
Alternative energy is the future.
Trust me, Mel.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.440
After seeing allinol in action
at the World Grand Prix,

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.320
nobody will ever go back
to gasoline again.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.400
What happened to the dinosaurs, now?

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.320
And on satellite,
a World Grand Prix competitor

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.600
and one of the fastest cars in the world,
Francesco Bernoulli.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.160
It is an honor, Signore Dorado,
for you.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.960
Why not invite Lightning McQueen?

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:30.600
Of course we invited him,

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.120
but apparently after his very long
racing season

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.200
he is taking time off to rest.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.760
The Lightning McQueen would not
have a chance against Francesco.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.960
I can go over 300 kilometers an hour.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.960
In miles, that is like...
way faster than McQueen.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.960
Let's go to the phones.
Baltimore, Maryland, you're on the air.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.360
-Am I on? Hello?
-You're on. Go ahead.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.760
-Hello?
-Go ahead.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:54.840
(LINE GOES DEAD)

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.440
Let's go to Radiator Springs.
You're on, caller.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.280
MATER: That Italian feller
you got on there

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.160
can't talk that way about
Lightning McQueen.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.480
He's the bestest race car
in the whole wide world.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.360
-Uh-oh.
-If he is, how you say,

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.360
"the bestest race car,"
then why must he rest? Huh?

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.000
MATER: 'Cause he knows
what's important.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.720
Every now and then he prefers
just to slow down, enjoy life.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.880
Oh! You heard it!
Lightning McQueen prefers to be slow!

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.720
This is not news to Francesco.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.120
When I want to go to sleep,
I watch one of his races.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.840
After two laps, I am out cold.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:28.120
-(MURMURING)
-MATER: That ain't what I meant.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.440
McQUEEN: What's going on
over there?

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.120
FRANCESCO:
He is afraid of Francesco.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.520
McQUEEN: That's that
Italian formula car.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.880
-His name is...
-Francesco Bernoulli.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.400
-No wonder there's a crowd.
-Why do you know his name?

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.320
And don't say it like that.
It's three syllables, not ten.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.880
What? He's nice to look at.
You know, open-wheeled and all.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.520
What's wrong with fenders?
I thought you liked my fenders.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.720
-Let me tell you something else.
-Mater?

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.360
MATER: McQueen could drive circles
around you.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.440
Driving in circles is all he can-a do,
no?

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:00.560
MATER: No.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.280
I mean, yes.
I mean, he could beat you anywhere.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.560
Any time, any track.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.560
Mel, can we move on?

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.520
Francesco needs a caller
who can provide

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.840
a little more intellectual stimulation,
like a dump truck.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.280
Ha-ha! That shows what you know.
Dump trucks is dumb.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.560
Hey! Whoa!

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.720
Yeah, hi. This is Lightning McQueen.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.720
The Lightning McQueen, huh?

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.280
I don't appreciate my best friend
being insulted like that.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.080
McQueen, that was your best friend?
Oh!

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.280
This is the difference
between you and Francesco.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.640
Francesco knows how good he is.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:37.000
He does not need to surround himself
with tow trucks to prove it.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:40.920
Those are strong words
from a car that is so fragile.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.000
Fragile! He calls Francesco fragile!

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.280
Not-a so fast, McQueen!

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.840
"Not so fast."
Is that your new motto?

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.880
Motto? (CONTINUES IN ITALIAN)

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.880
This sounds like something that needs
to be settled on the race course.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.000
What do you say, Lightning McQueen?
We've got room for one more racer.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.520
I would love to,
but my crew is off for the season, so...

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.440
(LUG NUTS POPPING)

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.480
Pit stop.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.920
You know what? They just got back.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.560
Deal me in, baby.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.000
-Ka-chow! Yeah.
-(CHEERING)

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.600
I know, I know.
I just got back, but we won't be long.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.440
No, don't worry about me.
I've got enough to do here.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.400
Mater's going to have a blast, though.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.240
You're bringing Mater, right?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:28.760
You never bring him
to any of your races.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.120
(SLURPS AND GULPS)

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.240
(MUFFLED CRIES)

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.440
(SLURPS) Ah.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.840
Just let him sit in the pits.
Give him a headset.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.280
Come on, it will be
the thrill of a lifetime for him.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.360
-Your drink, sir.
-Mater.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:43.800
I didn't taste it!

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.640
How'd you like to come
and see the world with me?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.600
-You mean it?
-Yeah. You got me into this thing.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.760
-You're coming along.
-All right!

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.520
(ENGINE REVS)

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.000
Ka-chow!

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.240
Ha-ha!

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.480
(JET ENGINE ROARS)

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.920
(BOTH LAUGH)

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.720
(BOTH LAUGH)

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.160
Hey!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.040
MATER: Hey, excuse me!

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.080
(IN JAPANESE)
Domo arigato!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.960
-Yeah!
-(LAUGHS)

